   103	applying the inclusion criteria, 537 secondary studies re-
   104	mained.
   105	2.3. Data extraction
   106	Data extraction from the PDF files of secondary stud-
   107	ies was conducted in two rounds: (1) manually and (2)
   108	automatically. In the manual phase, full-text screening is
   109	conducted for each included article to identify dedicated
   110	sections indicating the availability of research artifacts. In
   111	the automated phase, keyword search is conducted for the
   112	articles with a Python script that prints 100 characters be-
   113	fore and after each keyword occurrence, which are then
   114	manually checked. We checked if the paper contains a ref-
   115	erence to the external resource and if it is located in a per-
   116	manent repository, such as Figshare, Zenodo or Mende-
   117	ley.
   118	3. Results
   119	The results are shown in Table 1.
   120	RQ1: What proportion of secondary studies include
   121	a research artifact?RQ1 gives an overview of the avail-
   122	ability of research artifacts in SE SRs. Ideally, every sec-
   123	ondary study would include a research artifact accessi-
   124	ble through a direct link. Results: In our dataset, 169
   125	of the 537 (31.5%) reviewed secondary studies include a
   126	research artifact.
   127	RQ2: Where are the research artifacts stored?RQ2
   128	addresses the storage location for research artifacts. Re-
   129	search artifacts should be located in permanent storage
   130	with a digital object identifier (DOI). Links to personal or
   131	institutional web pages may stop working in a few years.
